  "decision": "replace_ranges",
  "evidence": "Original N/E/U shows a sustained ~5 mm N, ~-22 mm E, ~-2.5 mm U offset beginning near index 599 and persisting through ~638, followed by an opposing return (~-6 mm N, ~+21 mm E, ~+2.8 mm U) at index 638–639 (P4), consistent with a temporary platform. P1 (598–601) and P2 (599) are too short and overlap; P3 (600–638) captures the main sustained offset but excludes the clear return at 638. P5 (640–643) is post-return and likely unrelated motion or noise. The onset-offset estimates for P1–P3 align in direction and magnitude, while P4 opposes them, supporting a single temporary platform from ~599 to ~638 with return at 638. No independent permanent step is evident within this interval; physical motion (smooth trends before/after) is preserved.",
  "pair_ids": ["P3", "P4"]
}
